# Step-by-step installation.
tui.wizard.start = Installation wizard
tui.wizard.title = Installation wizard — step {0} of {1}
tui.wizard.back = Back
tui.wizard.next = Next
tui.wizard.close = Return to configuration
tui.wizard.step.0 = Paths: choose the server data folder and the client used as a source.
tui.wizard.step.1 = Storage: choose SQLite or an enabled database provider and enter its connection settings.
tui.wizard.step.2 = Components: choose map extraction and enter the realm name. An account is optional. Next checks storage and builds the plan.
tui.wizard.step.3 = Review: confirm the destination and operations before installation.
tui.wizard.step.4 = Installing: wait for preparation to finish. Esc cancels the operation.
tui.wizard.step.5 = Installation complete. The server can now be started separately.
tui.wizard.paths_note = Paths are relative to the YAML profile. A complete local WoW 3.3.5a client is required as a data source, including on a headless host. Install or enable optional plugins in Plugins before choosing their storage provider here.
tui.wizard.done = Saved profile: {0}. Use Plugins and Settings to configure plugin fields and LAN access. Then close the TUI and run LonelyIce --headless --settings with this profile.
